                        "entry_id": "2914b14a-9e59-3a25-ae17-8dd0dbc33f90",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A mischievous, potentially malicious fairy, akin to the leprechaun, that greatly loves drinking and tends to haunt breweries, pubs and wine cellars."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Irish"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d6dd5cb5-0294-4af4-8616-b8cd4aa406f3",
                                "sense_id": "422cff56-d23e-3e21-be81-d93f78ed66cd",
                                "text": "The residents of a house would leave offerings for the clurichaun, who sing in Gaelic with enchantingly beautiful voices. Related to leprechauns, clurichauns are house faeries who specialize in caring for and protecting wine and beer cellars."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fd8bf061-7fe9-4fc9-9aab-97c19935f788",
                                "sense_id": "422cff56-d23e-3e21-be81-d93f78ed66cd",
                                "text": "2016, Keith B. Darrell, Flashbacks: Fangs & Fur, Book 1, Amber Book Company, unnumbered page,\n\"Clurichauns are Dark Fae cousins of leprechauns,\" Aurae explained. \"Unlike their Seelie Court cousins, the clurichauns drink to excess and are seldom sober. But despite always being drunk, the clurichauns are impeccably groomed and well-dressed... although they can be a bit surly.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    }
